From efaf4e8a798c9f4959015372e0ba3101aa06ec19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: letress <212964567+letress@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:47:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 44/52] dt-bindings: clock: exynos9610: Use a 64 KiB region in
 the example

The driver sets auto_clock_gate for every CMU. The Samsung clock code
only honours that when the CMU's register region is 0x10000 long
(samsung_is_auto_capable()); with the 0x8000 from the example it prints
"incorrect res size for automatic clocks" and silently falls back to
manual gating, which is not what the driver asks for.

Automatic mode reads the gate state from the debug registers at offset
0x4000, the same offset and encoding the vendor kernel uses
(dbg_offset in cal-if/exynos9610/cmucal-sfr.c). None of the CMUs has a
neighbour within 64 KiB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos9610-cmu.yaml       | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos9610-cmu.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos9610-cmu.yaml
index 06d01b9..51d23a9 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos9610-cmu.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/samsung,exynos9610-cmu.yaml
@@ -318,7 +318,7 @@ examples:
 
     cmu_fsys: clock-controller@13400000 {
         compatible = "samsung,exynos9610-cmu-fsys";
-        reg = <0x13400000 0x8000>;
+        reg = <0x13400000 0x10000>;
         #clock-cells = <1>;
 
         clocks = <&oscclk>,
